WEBVTT

00:00:09.750 --> 00:00:13.790
Nothing dramatic is guaranteed to happen
just because it's Christmas.

00:00:13.790 --> 00:00:17.750
Today's not going to be
a great memory or anything.

00:00:20.910 --> 00:00:23.620
What exactly is Christmas?

00:00:25.700 --> 00:00:29.000
Just how grand is this phenomenon
known as Christmas?

00:00:31.080 --> 00:00:34.290
Is there a right way to celebrate Christmas?

00:00:36.290 --> 00:00:41.160
What is this luck that supposedly
comes with Christmas?

00:00:41.160 --> 00:00:45.700
Does something that's born
on Christmas shine bright?

00:00:45.700 --> 00:00:48.200
"Good Luck"

00:00:45.700 --> 00:00:48.200
What exactly are you
supposed to do on Christmas?

00:00:48.200 --> 00:00:50.580
What exactly are you
supposed to do on Christmas?

00:00:51.580 --> 00:00:52.950
Hey, now!

00:00:52.950 --> 00:00:55.830
Quit spacing out!

00:00:55.830 --> 00:00:59.410
Oh, sorry. U-Um, Manager?

00:00:59.410 --> 00:01:00.660
What is it?

00:01:00.660 --> 00:01:06.910
May I take Christmas...
May I take the 25th off?

00:01:06.910 --> 00:01:08.290
You got a date?

00:01:08.290 --> 00:01:11.330
I-I wouldn't exactly...

00:01:12.410 --> 00:01:14.580
...call it that...

00:02:47.000 --> 00:02:49.330
First off, is a date where you do

00:02:49.330 --> 00:02:55.910
something fun with someone you're
interested in to get closer to them?

00:02:55.910 --> 00:03:01.000
And in that case, I guess you could
sort of call this a date.

00:03:01.000 --> 00:03:05.120
My date with Shimamura...
What should we do on Christmas?

00:03:07.000 --> 00:03:10.290
Chicken, a cake, a tree,

00:03:10.290 --> 00:03:12.790
a present...

00:03:12.790 --> 00:03:14.000
Oh...

00:03:15.830 --> 00:03:18.700
A present for Shimamura.

00:03:20.080 --> 00:03:23.000
A present, a present...

00:03:23.000 --> 00:03:25.120
A Christmas present for Shimamura--

00:03:25.120 --> 00:03:30.540
Heya, Adachicchi! What're you spaced out for?
You feeling faint?

00:03:30.540 --> 00:03:32.700
It's not that.

00:03:32.700 --> 00:03:34.870
Oh, you must be waiting for Shimamura.

00:03:34.870 --> 00:03:37.000
No, not really...

00:03:37.000 --> 00:03:39.790
Hey, it's rare to see you alone.

00:03:39.790 --> 00:03:41.000
Wut?

00:03:41.000 --> 00:03:46.870
Oh, yeah. She's not here.
How did she lose me?

00:03:46.870 --> 00:03:49.450
Don't you need to wait for Nagafuji?

00:03:49.450 --> 00:03:54.580
I don't usually get the chance
to ask you out to lunch.

00:03:54.580 --> 00:03:56.910
Thanks for the grub!

00:03:56.910 --> 00:03:58.700
Let's eat.

00:04:04.750 --> 00:04:05.660
Say.

00:04:07.120 --> 00:04:10.620
Do you know what Shimamura likes?

00:04:10.620 --> 00:04:14.160
Does she have anything she actually likes?

00:04:15.290 --> 00:04:18.410
She's not the type of person that
actually talks about stuff like that.

00:04:18.410 --> 00:04:19.950
I know...

00:04:19.950 --> 00:04:23.410
Have you been shopping with Shimamura before?

00:04:23.410 --> 00:04:26.580
I have, but it's usually like a bookstore.

00:04:26.580 --> 00:04:29.950
Oh, and we've peeked in a tea shop before.

00:04:29.950 --> 00:04:30.830
Tea shop?

00:04:30.830 --> 00:04:35.830
Well, we went because of me,
but Shimamura did have a look, too.

00:04:35.830 --> 00:04:41.410
Oh, yeah. I think there was a certain tea
that she said smelled good.

00:04:41.410 --> 00:04:44.160
But I don't remember if it
was black tea or green...

00:04:44.160 --> 00:04:47.120
I see. So tea...

00:04:47.120 --> 00:04:50.160
You wouldn't happen to remember
the name of that tea, would you?

00:04:50.160 --> 00:04:53.830
Um... One sec.

00:04:53.830 --> 00:04:58.290
Man, what was it? It wasn't barley tea...

00:04:58.290 --> 00:05:00.870
Which shelf was it on...?

00:05:02.620 --> 00:05:04.830
Nope, I don't remember.

00:05:06.500 --> 00:05:09.450
The name is on the tip of my tongue, though.

00:05:09.450 --> 00:05:13.120
I think I can remember it if I see it again.

00:05:14.580 --> 00:05:18.410
If you see it... Um...

00:05:18.410 --> 00:05:21.950
Will you look for it with me?

00:05:21.950 --> 00:05:26.080
Hm. I mean, you could just
take Shimamura with you.

00:05:31.120 --> 00:05:33.620
Ah, I see.

00:05:33.620 --> 00:05:38.370
In that case, I'll go with you and choose.

00:05:38.370 --> 00:05:39.580
Really?

00:05:39.580 --> 00:05:42.410
There's Hino!

00:05:42.410 --> 00:05:47.870
There you are.
Where'd you get lost at, Nagafuji?

00:05:47.870 --> 00:05:49.580
Oh?

00:05:49.580 --> 00:05:51.250
H-Hey...

00:05:51.250 --> 00:05:54.540
Did you shrink?

00:05:54.540 --> 00:05:55.450
Wha...?

00:05:55.450 --> 00:06:00.790
It's just you seem smaller than usual,
so I lost track of you.

00:06:00.790 --> 00:06:03.080
--What'd you say?!
--Ow.

00:06:08.580 --> 00:06:10.250
Do you mind if I have some ramen?

00:06:10.250 --> 00:06:11.870
Hand over some bread, then.

00:06:11.870 --> 00:06:12.700
--There's a sweet one.

00:06:12.700 --> 00:06:13.290
--They're so close...
--There's a sweet one.

00:06:13.290 --> 00:06:14.660
--They're so close...
--Ooh, give me that one!

00:06:14.660 --> 00:06:16.620
Here.

00:06:16.620 --> 00:06:21.750
I don't think I'd ever... be able to smack
Shimamura on the head like that.

00:06:25.370 --> 00:06:26.870
Sorry!

00:06:26.870 --> 00:06:29.370
Adatty, have you been waiting long?

00:06:29.370 --> 00:06:31.120
Nagafuji's not with you?

00:06:31.120 --> 00:06:33.290
She apparently had something to do.

00:06:33.290 --> 00:06:37.200
She has a day like that like
once a year. Anyway, let's go!

00:06:37.200 --> 00:06:38.200
Okay.

00:06:39.200 --> 00:06:41.250
Oh... Do you want to get on the back?

00:06:41.250 --> 00:06:44.950
I will, but we should
get away from school first.

00:06:44.950 --> 00:06:47.700
If a teacher sees us,
we'll never hear the end of it.

00:06:47.700 --> 00:06:49.040
Wow...

00:06:49.040 --> 00:06:50.660
What?

00:06:50.660 --> 00:06:53.950
I never thought of you as an honor student.

00:06:56.370 --> 00:06:59.790
Praise me more.

00:06:59.790 --> 00:07:02.330
I bet it is pretty weird...

00:07:02.330 --> 00:07:05.620
That I'm imagining walking around town
on Christmas with another girl

00:07:05.620 --> 00:07:07.910
and my heart is about to burst.

00:07:07.910 --> 00:07:13.700
I'm sure that Shimamura isn't
this anxious about Christmas.

00:07:13.700 --> 00:07:17.410
There's definitely a difference in how
I feel about Shimamura and vice versa.

00:07:17.410 --> 00:07:22.620
And I'm not sure if I want her
to realize that... or not.

00:07:23.410 --> 00:07:24.620
"Jikkokuya Jyugoro"

00:07:24.620 --> 00:07:27.120
"Jikkokuya Jyugoro"

00:07:24.620 --> 00:07:27.120
Thank you for coming by again.

00:07:27.120 --> 00:07:28.330
"Jikkokuya Jyugoro"

00:07:27.120 --> 00:07:28.330
Heya.

00:07:28.830 --> 00:07:29.870
"Ginger Tea"

00:07:29.870 --> 00:07:31.200
"Ginger Tea"

00:07:29.870 --> 00:07:31.200
Do you come here often?

00:07:31.200 --> 00:07:35.660
Yeah... I may or may not have someone
in my family who drinks a lot of tea...

00:07:35.660 --> 00:07:38.950
Ginger... That'd probably warm you right up.

00:07:38.950 --> 00:07:41.410
Apparently, it works great
for people who get cold easily...

00:07:41.410 --> 00:07:43.370
According to my family member.

00:07:43.370 --> 00:07:44.830
You don't drink it?

00:07:44.830 --> 00:07:50.200
Well, I don't exactly get cold easily.
Let's see, where was it...?

00:07:50.200 --> 00:07:53.830
I'm pretty sure it was on this shelf...

00:08:09.910 --> 00:08:13.370
Hey, Adatty. Can I ask you something?

00:08:14.500 --> 00:08:17.830
Are you the type that would get mad
if I confidently told you,

00:08:17.830 --> 00:08:20.950
"Yeah, this is the one!" and was totally wrong?

00:08:20.950 --> 00:08:24.290
I don't think my personality sucks that badly...

00:08:24.290 --> 00:08:27.160
Oh, good. Then I think it's this one.

00:08:30.040 --> 00:08:36.620
Man... Thanks for treating me.
Though I sorta talked you into it.

00:08:36.620 --> 00:08:37.750
Sure...

00:08:37.750 --> 00:08:39.790
It's a bit chilly in here.

00:08:39.790 --> 00:08:41.500
My legs are freezing.

00:08:41.500 --> 00:08:42.790
Yeah.

00:08:44.000 --> 00:08:48.580
You're totally anxious because you
don't know what to say right now, huh?

00:08:48.580 --> 00:08:50.830
Y-Yeah...

00:08:50.830 --> 00:08:55.080
I'm sure it would've been the same
with Nagafuji here, too.

00:08:55.080 --> 00:08:57.750
Though, in her case...

00:08:57.750 --> 00:08:58.910
Huh?

00:09:18.790 --> 00:09:23.580
So that's what she had to do...
Did you know about this?

00:09:27.200 --> 00:09:31.000
Good grief. What am I going to do with you?

00:09:31.000 --> 00:09:33.200
Huh? What?

00:09:34.330 --> 00:09:36.410
Wanna follow them?

00:09:37.410 --> 00:09:40.950
Let's not. They seem busy.

00:09:40.950 --> 00:09:44.620
Ah, Adatty, always the honor student.

00:09:46.950 --> 00:09:49.750
I thought I was the only one...

00:09:49.750 --> 00:09:52.580
...that got to hang out
with Shimamura alone.

00:09:52.580 --> 00:09:55.370
"Why were you with Nagafuji?"

00:09:52.580 --> 00:09:55.370
...that got to hang out
with Shimamura alone.

00:09:55.580 --> 00:10:01.410
And the fact that I was totally wrong
about that shouldn't hurt this much.

00:10:03.200 --> 00:10:05.830
I'm so dumb.

00:10:05.830 --> 00:10:08.040
Shimamura...

00:10:08.040 --> 00:10:10.290
Just saying her name...

00:10:10.290 --> 00:10:15.830
Just the sound of her name was enough
to get me through this winter.

00:10:16.790 --> 00:10:18.370
Hey, hey, hey.

00:10:18.370 --> 00:10:20.370
Are you really an alien, Yachi?

00:10:20.370 --> 00:10:22.290
Tsk, tsk, tsk.

00:10:22.290 --> 00:10:25.700
But of course. I have never told a lie.

00:10:25.700 --> 00:10:28.540
Then show me proof!
Proof that you're an alien.

00:10:28.540 --> 00:10:29.950
Tsk, tsk, tsk.

00:10:29.950 --> 00:10:32.950
I would be violating my agreement
if I showed you, so I cannot.

00:10:32.950 --> 00:10:37.040
The rules of the universe
can be rather strict. Oh?

00:10:37.040 --> 00:10:40.750
What is that, Little Shimamura?

00:10:51.870 --> 00:10:55.370
My, my, my, what a dramatic sound...

00:10:55.370 --> 00:10:57.750
You're the one that's dramatic, Yachi.

00:10:57.750 --> 00:11:01.040
Just breathe into it more gently...

00:11:02.040 --> 00:11:05.750
Ah, it's almost discount time, so I must go.

00:11:10.250 --> 00:11:11.450
Huh?

00:11:18.080 --> 00:11:19.790
Alienspeak?

00:11:22.500 --> 00:11:25.950
Shimamura and I are just normal friends.

00:11:25.950 --> 00:11:28.700
At least, that's how Shimamura sees us.

00:11:28.700 --> 00:11:32.200
Even then, I still want to get
closer to Shimamura one step at a time.

00:11:32.200 --> 00:11:33.660
"I'm looking forward to tomorrow."
Even then, I still want to get
closer to Shimamura one step at a time.

00:11:33.660 --> 00:11:36.000
"I'm looking forward to tomorrow."
But the closer you get,
the more things get across.

00:11:36.000 --> 00:11:40.870
But the closer you get,
the more things get across.

00:11:40.870 --> 00:11:45.250
I keep mentioning Christmas
with Shimamura, but...

00:11:45.250 --> 00:11:48.910
Is it love? No, no, no...

00:11:48.910 --> 00:11:52.830
Romance? No, no, no...

00:11:52.830 --> 00:11:54.080
Like...?

00:11:59.540 --> 00:12:02.660
Whatever it is, it's warm and fuzzy.

00:12:02.660 --> 00:12:06.700
It's a warm liquid that flows through my chest.

00:12:20.450 --> 00:12:21.000
"Cool!"

00:12:21.000 --> 00:12:22.910
"Cool!"

00:12:21.000 --> 00:12:22.910
Huh?

00:12:22.910 --> 00:12:25.790
What's this "Cool" supposed to mean?

00:12:25.790 --> 00:12:29.000
Like, "Coolio"? Maybe she meant, "Chill out"?

00:12:29.000 --> 00:12:31.410
Or, "Cool beans"?

00:12:31.410 --> 00:12:33.370
"Cool!"

00:12:33.790 --> 00:12:37.830
I want to hear Shimamura's voice...

00:12:37.830 --> 00:12:40.370
I want to know more about her.

00:12:40.370 --> 00:12:43.450
And I'll be able to hear
and ask her lots tomorrow.

00:13:12.290 --> 00:13:13.870
Were you waiting long?

00:13:14.790 --> 00:13:16.330
I just got here.

00:13:16.330 --> 00:13:17.750
You liar.

00:13:17.750 --> 00:13:22.290
I've been watching you sitting here
for the last five minutes from afar.

00:13:22.290 --> 00:13:23.500
Huh?

00:13:25.040 --> 00:13:29.950
Er, I was just joking. Anyway,
sorry for making you wait.

00:13:29.950 --> 00:13:31.580
I-It's okay...

00:13:31.580 --> 00:13:36.870
So, I've been wondering
ever since I saw you today...

00:13:36.870 --> 00:13:39.080
Huh? What?

00:13:39.080 --> 00:13:43.620
Why are you wearing your Chinese dress
from work under your coat?

00:13:45.040 --> 00:13:48.790
Oh, uh... Yeah, I guess I can't
blame you for wondering.

00:13:48.790 --> 00:13:50.000
Actually,

00:13:50.000 --> 00:13:53.450
won't people think you're trying
to lure them into a sketchy shop?

00:13:54.450 --> 00:13:57.580
Look, even I know this is weird.

00:13:57.580 --> 00:14:02.620
But... She said I looked cute in it, so...

00:14:02.620 --> 00:14:07.660
Oh, I think it's fine. You look super cute.

00:14:07.660 --> 00:14:11.830
It must be nice being so pretty.
You can actually pull that outfit off.

00:14:11.830 --> 00:14:16.500
B-But you're even cuter Shimamura...

00:14:18.700 --> 00:14:21.250
You can skip the sarcasm.

00:14:21.250 --> 00:14:21.910
--Christmas all alone with Shimamura...

00:14:21.910 --> 00:14:24.500
--So, where are you taking me today?
--Christmas all alone with Shimamura...

00:14:24.500 --> 00:14:26.790
--Um, we should go to the 2nd floor.
--Though Shimamura's probably only here
because she felt obligated as a friend.

00:14:26.790 --> 00:14:29.830
--Though Shimamura's probably only here
because she felt obligated as a friend.

00:14:29.830 --> 00:14:34.580
I need to stop. Whenever I let my guard down,
my thoughts just go down a dark path

00:14:34.580 --> 00:14:37.040
and I'll get depressed...

00:14:46.750 --> 00:14:49.160
S-Sorry.

00:14:50.120 --> 00:14:53.580
No, really. I'm sorry.

00:14:55.160 --> 00:14:57.000
So, hey.

00:14:57.000 --> 00:15:00.620
Don't suddenly grab my hand
like a purse-snatcher.

00:15:00.620 --> 00:15:01.830
Sorry.

00:15:01.830 --> 00:15:03.620
Did you want to hold hands?

00:15:03.620 --> 00:15:05.540
If we could.

00:15:05.540 --> 00:15:09.120
Didn't we do this all before?

00:15:09.120 --> 00:15:10.500
Possibly.

00:15:20.450 --> 00:15:25.580
Next time, make sure you just ask if it's okay.

00:15:27.040 --> 00:15:29.500
Yus!

00:15:29.500 --> 00:15:33.250
What kind of response is that?
How did you even pronounce that?

00:15:33.250 --> 00:15:35.370
You might've sounded like a shrimp just now.

00:15:35.370 --> 00:15:38.870
Just ignore that. Um...

00:15:38.870 --> 00:15:41.830
I got it, though. I'll ask next time.

00:15:41.830 --> 00:15:43.450
Good.

00:15:43.910 --> 00:15:45.410
Come on.

00:15:47.790 --> 00:15:49.910
You don't need to panic so much.

00:15:49.910 --> 00:15:54.160
No one else is going to steal my hand from you.

00:15:59.000 --> 00:16:05.450
But I'm not the only one
that gets to walk next to you...

00:16:05.450 --> 00:16:07.370
I was thinking we could play here.

00:16:07.370 --> 00:16:09.830
Huh... An arcade.

00:16:09.830 --> 00:16:11.660
Oh, hey. A ping-pong table.

00:16:11.660 --> 00:16:15.000
Yeah, but I was thinking...

00:16:15.000 --> 00:16:18.950
We could play... this. Air hockey.
What do you think?

00:16:18.950 --> 00:16:21.370
Sure, why not?

00:16:21.370 --> 00:16:22.500
Okay.

00:16:23.870 --> 00:16:28.410
Air hockey is sort of similar
to ping-pong in some ways.

00:16:28.410 --> 00:16:29.330
--This was our pastime.

00:16:29.330 --> 00:16:31.290
--You can go first, Adachi.
--This was our pastime.

00:16:31.290 --> 00:16:31.870
--Okay, take that!

00:16:31.870 --> 00:16:35.790
--Okay, take that!
--Shimamura and I met
on the second floor of the gym.

00:16:35.790 --> 00:16:38.870
No matter how it happened, once we've met,

00:16:38.870 --> 00:16:42.370
there was a path that
led us there as well as fate.

00:16:44.290 --> 00:16:44.950
--No matter the encounter, there's always
a grand past that goes along with it.

00:16:44.950 --> 00:16:47.450
--This is sorta different.
--No matter the encounter, there's always
a grand past that goes along with it.

00:16:47.450 --> 00:16:49.040
--What do you mean?
--No matter the encounter, there's always
a grand past that goes along with it.

00:16:49.040 --> 00:16:52.950
--I play the video game version
of this at home with my sister,
--Two hundred, 500, billions of
actions done by everyone and everything

00:16:52.950 --> 00:16:55.750
--and it's definitely a bit different.
--Two hundred, 500, billions of
actions done by everyone and everything

00:16:55.750 --> 00:16:58.410
piled up together in order
for two people to meet.

00:16:58.410 --> 00:17:01.500
I wonder what kind of paths led us to meet.

00:17:01.500 --> 00:17:07.580
Even one different decision would've meant
that I wouldn't have met Shimamura.

00:17:07.580 --> 00:17:10.370
And that fact alone...

00:17:11.540 --> 00:17:15.500
Made me endlessly like my past self.

00:17:15.500 --> 00:17:19.200
Y-You're pretty good at this, Adachi...

00:17:19.200 --> 00:17:22.080
H-How you like them apples?

00:17:24.910 --> 00:17:27.620
Jeez, Adachi. You're super good.

00:17:27.620 --> 00:17:30.500
I never expected you to be
the type to pick on noobs.

00:17:30.500 --> 00:17:32.660
It's not like that.

00:17:32.660 --> 00:17:35.330
I think you also had more wins
in ping-pong, too.

00:17:35.330 --> 00:17:36.750
Did I?

00:17:36.750 --> 00:17:39.700
Wait, maybe it's me.

00:17:39.700 --> 00:17:44.000
It's not fair to make stuff up
just because I don't remember.

00:17:44.000 --> 00:17:49.370
But it doesn't seem that long ago somehow.

00:17:49.370 --> 00:17:54.080
When spring comes and we become second-years
and the sun is out more again,

00:17:54.080 --> 00:17:56.950
I wonder if we're gonna go to the gym again.

00:18:02.120 --> 00:18:08.750
I think we can just go to class,
come here after school, and play ping-pong.

00:18:08.750 --> 00:18:13.370
A perfect score. You're a total
honor student now, Adachi.

00:18:15.370 --> 00:18:19.620
But man, we're gonna be second-years...
We'll probably be in different classes.

00:18:23.660 --> 00:18:25.870
Shimamura... here.

00:18:27.000 --> 00:18:31.120
I bought you a Christmas gift... or something...

00:18:31.120 --> 00:18:35.950
Wow... Well, this was a nice surprise.
Can I open it?

00:18:35.950 --> 00:18:37.580
Yeah.

00:18:37.580 --> 00:18:42.370
Oh, hey. This is the nice smelling one.
I wanted to try it out.

00:18:42.370 --> 00:18:44.040
This is great!

00:18:45.040 --> 00:18:48.290
But how did you know I liked this?

00:18:49.700 --> 00:18:50.870
Just a coincidence?

00:18:50.870 --> 00:18:52.160
No...

00:18:52.160 --> 00:18:57.700
Hm... Oh, you must've asked Hino.

00:18:57.700 --> 00:18:59.580
Y-Yeah.

00:18:59.580 --> 00:19:04.040
You really didn't have to, Adachi.
But thank you.

00:19:05.790 --> 00:19:09.250
I never thought you'd be
thinking the same thing.

00:19:09.250 --> 00:19:10.500
Huh?

00:19:11.500 --> 00:19:13.540
Since you're such a good little girl, Adachi,

00:19:13.540 --> 00:19:16.660
Big Sis got you a present, too.

00:19:29.370 --> 00:19:30.870
What is that?

00:19:30.870 --> 00:19:35.120
A boomerang... Oh, and some goggles.

00:19:35.120 --> 00:19:36.950
Am I supposed to wear it
when I throw this thing?

00:19:36.950 --> 00:19:40.830
Yeah. Oh, I threw it
a few times before buying it.

00:19:40.830 --> 00:19:43.250
It's way more fun than you'd expect.

00:19:43.250 --> 00:19:48.000
I suck at choosing stuff like this,
so I asked Nagafuji to help me pick.

00:19:48.000 --> 00:19:49.580
Huh?

00:19:49.580 --> 00:19:52.040
Maybe she'd want a boomerang.

00:19:54.250 --> 00:19:58.040
I think kids would love them. They're super fun.

00:19:58.040 --> 00:20:01.410
Though they tend to snap when you
throw them around in winter.

00:20:01.410 --> 00:20:06.120
Oh, I just told Nagafuji I was getting
a present for my little sister.

00:20:06.120 --> 00:20:11.410
Nagafuji... I see.
So that's why she was with her...

00:20:12.410 --> 00:20:14.330
Adachi?

00:20:14.330 --> 00:20:18.950
Thanks... I'll take really good care of this.

00:20:18.950 --> 00:20:23.870
Honestly, I didn't care
about the boomerang, but...

00:20:23.870 --> 00:20:29.040
The fact that Shimamura gave this to me...
was the best gift I could ask for.

00:20:32.620 --> 00:20:36.330
So, yeah. You hold the boomerang behind you,

00:20:36.330 --> 00:20:40.750
and then throw it in front of you like you're
going to chop something vertically.

00:20:40.750 --> 00:20:45.040
Yeah, like that. Make sure you
don't throw it up, though.

00:20:59.290 --> 00:21:01.540
Well, it's your first try.

00:21:01.540 --> 00:21:04.120
Were you able to catch it, Shimamura?

00:21:04.120 --> 00:21:09.410
Yeah. But that's not bad for a beginner.

00:21:10.700 --> 00:21:13.000
But you sorta look like you're in some movie,

00:21:13.000 --> 00:21:16.410
throwing that thing in your Chinese dress.
It's very cinematic.

00:21:16.410 --> 00:21:17.830
Huh?!

00:21:25.830 --> 00:21:27.330
Hup.

00:21:35.000 --> 00:21:37.200
Not feeling it?

00:21:37.200 --> 00:21:38.160
Yeah...

00:21:38.160 --> 00:21:43.500
I see. Hey, should I go back
and buy you something else?

00:21:43.500 --> 00:21:46.160
No, no. I really like it.

00:21:46.160 --> 00:21:47.370
I see.

00:21:47.370 --> 00:21:51.950
But we probably should head back.
It's warmer inside.

00:21:57.700 --> 00:22:00.790
This was my only chance, I thought...

00:22:00.790 --> 00:22:02.620
Here, where no one else was around...

00:22:02.620 --> 00:22:06.750
This was the only place I'd be able to say
something like this to Shimamura...

00:22:06.750 --> 00:22:08.790
So I'm going to take it.

00:22:08.790 --> 00:22:12.750
Even if I'm not ready...
Even if I fall on my face...

00:22:12.750 --> 00:22:14.040
Shimamura.

00:22:19.580 --> 00:22:20.870
Huh?

00:22:22.540 --> 00:22:24.200
Adachi?

00:22:25.870 --> 00:22:28.290
I...

00:22:28.290 --> 00:22:31.660
I really like you, Shimamura...

00:22:31.660 --> 00:22:35.950
Like, really like you... love you...

00:22:41.910 --> 00:22:46.410
Shimamura, I...

00:22:52.370 --> 00:22:55.580
...want to be your friend...

00:22:55.580 --> 00:22:58.000
I'm pretty sure we already are?

00:22:58.000 --> 00:23:01.620
No, not just friends...

00:23:01.620 --> 00:23:04.660
But I want to be like, your best friend.

00:23:04.660 --> 00:23:06.250
My best friend?

00:23:06.250 --> 00:23:09.450
I sorta really want to be that, so...

00:23:09.450 --> 00:23:12.250
I'll do my best.

00:23:12.250 --> 00:23:14.500
I-I see...

00:23:18.500 --> 00:23:20.290
I don't really get it,

00:23:20.290 --> 00:23:24.410
but it's great that you're so ambitious.

00:23:24.410 --> 00:23:26.290
Y-Yeah!

00:23:26.290 --> 00:23:29.950
Nothing dramatic is guaranteed to happen
just because it's Christmas.

00:23:29.950 --> 00:23:34.040
Today's not going to be
a great memory or anything.

00:23:34.040 --> 00:23:37.040
I mean, my mind just kept going blank,

00:23:37.040 --> 00:23:39.790
so I didn't really have a chance
to remember anything.

00:23:42.700 --> 00:23:46.330
Just like scenery being covered in snow...

00:23:49.870 --> 00:23:52.000
I'm just going to carve the memory of
a white album into the back of my brain.

00:23:52.000 --> 00:23:55.370
"Episode 6: 'White Album'"

00:23:52.000 --> 00:23:55.370
I'm just going to carve the memory of
a white album into the back of my brain.

00:23:55.370 --> 00:23:57.950
"Episode 6: 'White Album'"

00:23:57.950 --> 00:23:58.830
"Next Time:
'Please Choose the Best Chocolate for Me'"

00:23:58.830 --> 00:24:01.250
"Next Time:
'Please Choose the Best Chocolate for Me'"

00:23:58.830 --> 00:24:01.250
Adashimapedia: Christmas.

00:24:01.250 --> 00:24:04.370
--What are you mad about, Hino?
--I'm not.

00:24:04.370 --> 00:24:06.620
Want some chicken curry
at my place on Christmas?

00:24:06.620 --> 00:24:08.330
It's Christmas, so chicken curry?

00:24:08.330 --> 00:24:10.250
Yup. It's a Nagafuji family tradition.

00:24:10.250 --> 00:24:13.000
I see. Guess I'll just have to come over then!
